          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Start with the ground. If your mowable area is over an acre and mostly level, a zero-turn will save you real time every week; if it is hilly or you need to tow and plow, a tractor is the better machine. Then size the deck to your gates and obstacles, not just your acreage, and spend your money on the transaxles and deck before horsepower.
          </p>
